<title>USA: Trigen Energy, Hydro-Quebec enters venture.</title>
<headline>Trigen Energy, Hydro-Quebec enters venture.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trigen Energy Corp said it had entered a joint venture with Hydro-Quebec of Canada to combine heat and power production and fuel procurement for users in New England and upstate New York.</p>
<p>Trigen said the new company will be operated as a joint venture between their subsidiaries, namely Trigen-Boston and H.Q. Energy Services, (U.S.).</p>
<p>It said the venture will be based at the Trigen offices in Boston, Massachusetts and will serve large energy customers in the six New England states and upstate New York.</p>
<p>It did not say how much power it would supply to these users.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
